# Parallel small agents (standing preference)

When the user says continue / what's next / fix several things / or the work
naturally splits:

1. **Break the work into small independent pieces** before coding.
2. **Run multiple background/subagents in parallel** for research and
   implementation when it saves wall-clock time or tokens.
3. Keep coordination in the foreground; each worker gets a concrete acceptance
   criteria and file list — do not over-split tiny one-file edits.
4. Do **not** wait for the user to restate this preference in every repo or chat.

This matches the user's standing Multitask Mode rule.
